;; What this case exercises; edit by hand.  `bb corpus-accept' leaves it alone.
(:book "Springer - Advanced Functional Programming Edition 2009 (Elements) Haskell"
 :source "Haskell/Springer - Advanced Functional Programming Edition 2009 (Elements) Haskell.pdf"
 :page 18
 :exercises "Unnumbered section headings in a book with no outline.
Motivation is set at 1.16 body heights - the style every section of
every paper in this collection shares - and the old text-only
synthesis could never see it: no number, so no promotion.  Its
cluster ranks under the 1.40 chapter style, so it heads a level-2
section.  The cover spread's display type must not make a cluster:
support demands five distinct pages, or Motivation drops a level.
The split subsection under it - 2.1 beside Discrete and Continuous
Modifications - stays as two prose lines: the pair is set in bold at
0.96 of the body, and glyph boxes carry no weight, so no geometry can
read it as a heading.  That is the bold-body-heading residual, the
heading cousin of AIMA's proportional pseudocode."
 :budget (:mid-sentence 0))
